course: dictionary
lesson: 1816
title: Clumsiness and clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Clumsiness is a noun. It is the name for the state of being clumsy, which means moving in an awkward, careless way so that you drop, bump into or break things. «Through clumsiness» means it happened because someone was careless, not on purpose.
explain: The word can also describe how someone says or does things. «Sorry for my clumsiness» is what you say after you have done or said something awkward that upset someone. Look at the words around the word to see which meaning fits.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Yawning, heavy eyes and clumsiness are signs of tiredness.» The three signs are listed together, so clumsiness must be a sign of being tired, like yawning. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: Clumsiness is a noun: it names a quality, the state of being clumsy.
fact: Clumsiness is uncountable, so you say «a lot of clumsiness», not «a lot of clumsinesses».
fact: «Through clumsiness» means by accident, because someone was careless.
fact: Clumsiness can be a sign of tiredness: children your age need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep a night.
fact: Clumsiness can also be a warning sign that the body is getting dangerously cold, called hypothermia.
exercise: «Yawning, heavy eyes and clumsiness are signs of tiredness.» In this sentence, what is clumsiness? | A loud noise made by a drum | A tasty pudding made with cream | A new bike with a bell | *A sign that you are tired
exercise: Ava says, «Sorry for my clumsiness» after she spills the juice. What does clumsiness mean here? | Feeling happy about the mess | Being very good at sport | *Moving in an awkward, careless way that makes things spill | Being quiet and shy
exercise: Find and copy the one word that names the danger in this sentence: «Strong shivering, slurred words and clumsiness are warning signs that the body is getting dangerously cold, called hypothermia.» | slurred | *hypothermia | shivering | clumsiness
test: Clumsiness is which part of speech? | verb | *noun | adverb | adjective
test: What does «through clumsiness» mean? | *By accident, because someone was careless | On purpose, to be funny | Very slowly and carefully | By magic
exam: Read this: «Heavy eyes, yawning and clumsiness are signs of tiredness; children need 9 to 12 hours of sleep.» Why does this sentence help you understand clumsiness? | It tells you clumsiness is a kind of sleep | The sleep hours show clumsiness is a fun game | *The signs listed with it show that clumsiness is a sign of tiredness | It has no clues at all
